review_comments:
As I understand it, arch_timing_counter_get() uses k_cycle_get_32() because we can not be certain that architecture supports k_cycle_get_64().

What if we did something like ...

```
timing_t arch_timing_counter_get(void)
{
#if CONFIG_TIMER_HAS_64BIT_CYCLE_COUNTER
	return k_cycle_get_64();
#else
	return k_cycle_get_32();
#endif
}

uint64_t arch_timing_cycles_get(volatile timing_t *const start,
				volatile timing_t *const end)
{
#if CONFIG_TIMER_HAS_64BIT_CYCLE_COUNTER
	return (*end - *start);
#else
	return ((uint32_t)*end - (uint32_t)*start);
#endif

}
```

This would then allow us to get the 64-bit behavior if it is available, but still fall back to 32-bit behavior if it is not.
